# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings or they break on Linux
# (bash errors on a `\r` in the shebang / commands), regardless of a
# contributor's core.autocrlf setting.
*.sh text eol=lf

# ── GitHub's language bar ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ardon-R2 is Rust, with no C. Everything else in the tree is either an
# R2 script, a reference harness in another language (the comparisons
# against R, PyTorch and JAX that back the accuracy and speed claims), a
# test input, or packaging — none of it is the product, and linguist
# should not count it as such.
#
# `.r2` is one of Rebol's extensions in linguist's table, so R2's own
# scripts were being reported as "Rebol". Linguist has no R2 entry; R is
# the honest nearest, since R2 scripts are R.
*.r2  linguist-language=R
*.r   linguist-language=R
# Reference harnesses and the R inputs of the differential test: needed
# to measure R2, not part of it.
benchmarks/**           linguist-documentation
tests/differential/**   linguist-documentation
# Packaging and CI glue.
installer/**            linguist-vendored
.github/**              linguist-vendored
*.ps1                   linguist-vendored
*.sh                    linguist-vendored
